    "title": "Slocomb man killed by State Trooper after high-speed chase - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Jessica Gauthier No media credit provided. ,\n1 hours ago\nDOTHAN, Ala. ( WDHN )– A Slocomb man was shot and killed by police in the Panhandle after a high-speed chase.\nEarly Wednesday morning a Florida State Trooper attempted to conduct a traffic stop in Washington County when the suspect took off.\nIt happened on State Road 79 near County Road 279 where the suspect was driving over 100 miles per hour in a 35MPH zone in the Vernon area.\nA pursuit began and a second State Trooper, along with deputies from the Washington County Sheriff’s Office, responded to assist.\nThe initial Trooper pulled a pit maneuver and the suspect took off on foot. Authorities say he was armed and saying things about having “charges” and that he was “going to death row.”\nTroopers were able to catch up with him in the woods, where they say he was threatening their lives with a firearm. Law enforcement then took action, and the suspect was shot by a Florida State Trooper.\nThe suspect has been identified as Joshua Haire, 27, of Slocomb, Alabama. Haire was pronounced dead at the scene.\nThis case is currently under investigation.\nStay with WDHN for updates.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WDHN - wdhn.com.",
